{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"concise-deplorable-gerenuk","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Summary\n\n10 `rebar doctor --repair` tests fail in a sandboxed environment because they resolve\ngit identity through the **configured repo root** rather than through the disposable\ntracker root the test actually creates. When the ambient user has no git `user.email`\nreachable from that root, the repair run aborts with a missing-git-email error.\n\nThese failures are **pre-existing** and were masked, not caused, by bug `985f`. While\nremediating `985f` a production change was made to `src/rebar/_commands/doctor.py`\n(`run_repair` passing the tracker directory as the repair-pause root when `repo_root`\nis `None`). Code review blocked that change on two independent grounds: it is a\nbehavioural regression in `doctor --repair` identity resolution, and it is out of scope\nfor a test-harness ticket. It was reverted, which re-exposed these 10 failures.\n\nThe conftest ambient-git-config scrub added by `985f` is sufficient for the\n`985f`-scoped cases — the direct repair-pause ownership tests pass with `doctor.py`\nreverted. These 10 older tests are a distinct defect with its own root cause.\n\n## Affected tests\n\n`tests/unit/test_doctor_dirty_tree.py`:\n\n- `test_doctor_repair_heals_the_seeded_wedge_end_to_end`\n- `test_class3_only_store_gets_no_mutation_and_no_backup_ref`\n- `test_repair_lock_discipline_two_windows`\n- `test_no_backup_ref_means_no_mutation`\n- `test_failed_mutations_are_unrepairable_and_fail_the_run`\n\n`tests/unit/test_doctor.py`:\n\n- `test_repair_force_writes_the_pre_repair_tag_and_repoints_it`\n- `test_run_repair_does_not_hold_a_lock_that_blocks_its_own_writes`\n- `test_json_output_carries_the_documented_finding_fields`\n- `test_repair_refuses_while_a_reconciler_pass_is_in_flight`\n- `test_unrepairable_finding_leaves_its_edge_and_the_run_continues`\n\n## Observed behaviour\n\nWith `doctor.py` at its unmodified state and the `985f` conftest scrub in place, the\nabove 10 tests fail with a missing git email during the repair run. They contribute 10\nof the 32 residual failures in a full sandboxed `make test`.\n\n## Investigation notes\n\nThe reviewer's objection to the reverted change is the starting point, not a proposed\nfix: `config.repo_root(explicit=tracker)` returns `Path(tracker).resolve()` verbatim,\nso substituting the tracker directory changes production identity resolution rather\nthan correcting the tests. The fix belongs in whichever layer makes these tests supply\ntheir own identity, and the correct layer must be established by investigation before\nany change is written. Do not re-apply the reverted production edit.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The root cause is confirmed by experiment and recorded as a comment on this\n      ticket, naming the exact call path by which the repair run resolves identity\n      through the configured repo root instead of the disposable tracker root, with\n      the failing assertion or error output quoted as evidence.\n- [ ] A failing test is written first and observed to fail for the identified root\n      cause before any fix is applied; the pre-fix failure output is recorded on this\n      ticket.\n- [ ] All 10 named tests pass in a sandboxed environment with no ambient git\n      `user.email` reachable from the configured repo root, verified by running those\n      exact node IDs and reporting the pytest summary line.\n- [ ] `src/rebar/_commands/doctor.py` behaviour for `run_repair` with an explicit\n      `repo_root` is unchanged, verified by the existing repair-pause ownership tests\n      passing unmodified and by showing the diff touches no production identity\n      resolution, or — if a production change proves genuinely necessary — by a\n      recorded justification on this ticket naming the behaviour that changes and why\n      the reviewer's regression objection does not apply.\n- [ ] `make lint` and `make typecheck` pass, reported with their exit status.\n- [ ] The full sandboxed `make test` residual failure count drops by exactly 10 from\n      the pre-fix baseline of 32, with the new count and its composition recorded on\n      this ticket.","id":"8c5f-7727-ed1c-4151","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"doctor repair tests resolve git identity through the configured repo root"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1789703460434515369,"uuid":"779c20e2-4cfc-4771-9770-3af0472aae38"}